From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:57:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] core, web: saved hardware-file versions come from GET
 /api/config/history

Why: controls_history was a socket command that only read the store's
history files, answered by the second dispatcher before the command
lock. Original Apertar serves a library read as a GET route on the web
server's thread with no command lock, and one item through a query
parameter (GET /api/presets, queryParameterValue, App:7360 and
App:7198-7199 @upstream-1.6.0; WEB-4, WEB-5).

What: handleWebRequest has GET /api/config/history next to
GET /api/config. Without ?name= it returns revision and history (name,
saved_at, by, revision), newest first. With ?name= it returns name and
text, or 404 with "No saved version called <name>.". The
controls_history block and its help entry are gone. The page reads
both through one fetchConfigHistory(name), which throws Core's
sentence like the other library fetches; Config history, the Undo
button and loadControlsHistory use it.

Tested: check_core.sh both tests PASS (warning count unchanged, 1,
not in these lines). --simulate with its own hardware file: curl list,
one version, an unknown name (404 + sentence), controls_history now
"Unknown command". Playwright on --simulate: Config history lists the
saved versions, picking one puts its text in the editor, an unknown
name toasts the sentence, Controls Undo restores the file. smoke diff:
only help (-1) and controls_history (now an error) changed.
controls_page_test.js mocks the old command; its copy moves the mock
to the route. Camera: nothing beyond the page check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
